# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository AND in every working tree.
#
# eol=lf is deliberate, not cosmetic: GitHub's Windows runners check out with
# core.autocrlf=true, so without it the same file is LF on macOS/Linux and CRLF
# on Windows. The QA suites assert on source text, and several of them match
# multi-line literals - those silently stop matching under CRLF. That mismatch
# has produced real CI failures and a legacy QA chain that cannot pass on any
# platform. Pinning the working tree to LF removes the whole class.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by that normalization.
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.node  binary
*.zip   binary
*.dmg   binary
*.icns  binary
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
